## Room for four

At twenty-six square metres this is the largest room in the house, and the extra space is the point: two large beds sit well apart with room to walk between them, so four people can share without anyone living out of a case in a doorway.

The far wall opens on to a balcony through a glazed door, and that is what stops the room feeling like a dormitory. Sage green runs throughout, plain on one wall and in the hotel's geometric pattern on the other, with a tall timber-clad unit framing the head of one bed and holding the wardrobe. A black console carries the coffee machine, the kettle and cups; there is a velvet stool tucked underneath, a radiator beneath the window, and the flat-screen TV is wall-mounted and clear of everything else.

The bathroom has a corner shower, a wall-hung basin and a heated towel rail.

Safe, iron and a full wardrobe are standard, alongside the seating area, television and coffee facilities found in every room. With four of you it is worth knowing that breakfast is served at the front of the hotel from 07:30 to 10:30 at seventeen fifty a head, 10% less when you have booked direct, and that the lobby puts out drinks and snacks on the house from the afternoon onwards.

The Albert Cuypmarkt is at the end of the street and the Museumplein is five minutes away by tram.
